/ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;">The weighted average interest rates on short-term bank borrowings as of December 31, 2024 and 2025 were <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_XH5U-e4P3EyaYDdbgpgGqw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2024_pmlv5TIJ9UukeZDo-Hvb4g" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ShortTermDebtWeightedAverageInterestRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_-TBf_FF5nUGFlukfGM84-g">1.20</ix:nonFraction>% and <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_XH5U-e4P3EyaYDdbgpgGqw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_E-ihm-r0uEmc93_y_fK3EQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ShortTermDebtWeightedAverageInterestRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_0Dc2kth6rES_Kha-AIG9Wg">1.13</ix:nonFraction>%, respectively. The weighted average interest rate on long-term bank borrowings as of December 31, 2025 was <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_XH5U-e4P3EyaYDdbgpgGqw" contextRef="As_Of_12_31_2025_E-ihm-r0uEmc93_y_fK3EQ" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:LongtermDebtWeightedAverageInterestRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_CkVZp8L5z0OjzYVSeKpWIA">2.40</ix:nonFraction>%.</p></ix:nonNumeric><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_5thzZQv0lEmmjN0BhcOUQA" name="zto:ConvertibleDebtTextBlock" id="Tb_LJfxrmMiTE2oHd4A13WG2Q" continuedAt="Tb_LJfxrmMiTE2oHd4A13WG2Q_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">11. Convertible Senior Notes</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">On August 29, 2022, the Company issued US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_qF0kSPXROUmXco8Ic_aVpw" contextRef="As_Of_8_29_2022_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_ConvertibleDebtMember_LjDnbg1haU-VhXoizYGg3A" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFaceAmount" scale="3" id="Narr_gnzG_9Jzb0ufrteTRoBp3Q">1,000,000</ix:nonFraction> of Convertible Senior Notes (&#8220;the Notes&#8221;). The Notes will mature on September 1, 2027 and bear interest at a rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_XH5U-e4P3EyaYDdbgpgGqw" contextRef="As_Of_8_29_2022_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_ConvertibleDebtMember_LjDnbg1haU-VhXoizYGg3A" decimals="INF" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentInterestRateStatedPercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_n9bQNkgHBkCi2XHOQazepQ">1.5</ix:nonFraction>% per year, payable semiannually in arrears on March 1 and September 1 of each year, beginning on March 1, 2023.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Holders of the Notes have the option to convert the Notes, in integral multiples of US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_qF0kSPXROUmXco8Ic_aVpw" contextRef="As_Of_8_29_2022_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_ConvertibleDebtMember_LjDnbg1haU-VhXoizYGg3A" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zto:DebtInstrumentPrincipalAmountDenominationForConversionIntoCommonStock" scale="3" id="Narr_ANEu-PodqEKsGRE2XzIquA">1</ix:nonFraction> principal amount, at any time prior to the close of business on the fifth scheduled trading day immediately preceding the maturity date. The Notes can be converted into the Company&#8217;s ADSs at an initial conversion rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_XH5U-e4P3EyaYDdbgpgGqw" contextRef="Duration_8_29_2022_To_8_29_2022_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_ConvertibleDebtMember_ZViqX_p2WUG1tXP2LiCzzA" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentConvertibleConversionRatio1" scale="0" id="Narr_kkh0uEpT6EeF97V83RgN8w">31.6296</ix:nonFraction> of the Company&#8217;s ADSs per US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_qF0kSPXROUmXco8Ic_aVpw" contextRef="As_Of_8_29_2022_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_ConvertibleDebtMember_LjDnbg1haU-VhXoizYGg3A" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zto:DebtInstrumentPrincipalAmountDenominationForConversionIntoCommonStock" scale="3" id="Narr_EN_UN1Aabk-7OkAOLYNDaw">1</ix:nonFraction> principal amount of the Notes (equivalent to an initial conversion price of US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_8k9rXZEOFkCLow36Uyv2xQ" contextRef="As_Of_8_29_2022_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_ConvertibleDebtMember_LjDnbg1haU-VhXoizYGg3A" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentConvertibleConversionPrice1" scale="0" id="Narr_O-3r3pDJVESfH_ZkKwFVpA">31.62</ix:nonFraction> per ADS). The conversion rate is subject to customary adjustments upon the occurrence of certain events, such as the payment of dividends. Upon conversion, the Company will pay or deliver, as the case may be, cash, ADSs, or a combination of cash and ADSs, at its selection. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The holders may require the Company to repurchase for cash all or part of the Notes on September 2, 2025 (the &#8220;repurchase date&#8221;) at a repurchase price equal to <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_XH5U-e4P3EyaYDdbgpgGqw" contextRef="Duration_8_29_2022_To_8_29_2022_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_ConvertibleDebtMember_ZViqX_p2WUG1tXP2LiCzzA" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentRedemptionPricePercentage" scale="-2" id="Narr_2cfTR2vshUS40KAZP8f9eQ">100</ix:nonFraction>% of the principal amount of the notes to be repurchased, plus accrued and unpaid interest to, but excluding, the relevant repurchase date. On September 2, 2025, the Company repurchased an aggregate principal amount of US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_qF0kSPXROUmXco8Ic_aVpw" contextRef="As_Of_9_2_2025_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_ConvertibleDebtMember_d1DSMst0NU6XazSgHSgDCQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentRepurchasedFaceAmount" scale="3" id="Narr_-uRdlHGXbk2Yk3PphhG6OQ">982,252</ix:nonFraction> (RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_xSGriXam1kKF-vMyssHgcw" contextRef="As_Of_9_2_2025_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_ConvertibleDebtMember_d1DSMst0NU6XazSgHSgDCQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentRepurchasedFaceAmount" scale="3" id="Narr_nj1TjJbYsES_wWgzaXhvnA">7,003,850</ix:nonFraction>) for the Notes. Following settlement of the repurchase, the aggregate principal amount of US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_qF0kSPXROUmXco8Ic_aVpw" contextRef="As_Of_9_2_2025_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_ConvertibleDebtMember_d1DSMst0NU6XazSgHSgDCQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:ConvertibleLongTermNotesPayable" scale="3" id="Narr_ls1cIBtwNkiC7yhyWzwecw">17,748</ix:nonFraction> for the Notes remain outstanding and were reclassified as non-current liabilities as the Notes will mature on September 1, 2027.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">The Company did not identify any embedded features that are subject to separate accounting. The conversion option meets the scope exception for derivative accounting as it is indexed to the Company&#8217;s own stock and classified in stockholders&#8217; equity. Other embedded features including the mandatory redemption feature and the contingent put option upon tax events or fundamental changes are considered clearly and closely related to the debt host with no separate accounting required.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;">Therefore, the Company accounted for the Notes as a single liability under convertible senior note, non-current. Issuance costs related to the Notes were recorded in consolidated balance sheet as a direct deduction from the principal amount of the Notes, and the discount caused by issuance cost is amortized over the period from August 29, 2022, the date of issuance, to September 2, 2025, the first put date of the Notes, using the effective interest method.</p></ix:nonNumeric></div><div style="clear:both;margin-bottom:30pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:24pt 0pt 0pt 0pt;">F-33</p></div></div>
<div style="background-color:#000000;clear:both;height:2pt;page-break-after:always;width:88.24%;border:0;margin:30pt 5.88% 30pt 5.88%;"></div><div style="max-width:100%;padding-left:5.88%;padding-right:5.88%;position:relative;"><div style="margin-top:21.6pt;min-height:14.4pt;width:100%;"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt 0pt 20pt 0pt;"><a href="#TOC"><span style="font-style:normal;font-weight:normal;">Table of Contents</span></a></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">ZTO EXPRESS (CAYMAN)&#160;INC. </b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">NOTES TO CONSOLIDATED FINANCIAL STATEMENTS </b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">FOR THE YEARS ENDED </b><b style="font-family:'Times New Roman Bold';font-weight:bold;text-transform:uppercase;">December</b><b style="font-weight:bold;"> 31, 2023, 2024 and 2025</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:center;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">(Amounts in thousands, except for share and per share data, unless otherwise stated)</b></p></div><div style="clear:both;max-width:100%;position:relative;background:#ffffff;"><ix:continuation id="Tb_LJfxrmMiTE2oHd4A13WG2Q_cont1"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 0pt;"><b style="font-weight:bold;">11. Convertible Senior Notes (Continued)</b></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;margin:0pt 0pt 12pt 36pt;"><span style="font-style:italic;font-weight:bold;">Capped Call Options</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;">In connection with the Notes, the Company entered into privately-negotiated capped call transactions indexed to its own ordinary shares with certain financial institutions based on the total offering US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_qF0kSPXROUmXco8Ic_aVpw" contextRef="As_Of_8_29_2022_us-gaap_LongtermDebtTypeAxis_us-gaap_ConvertibleDebtMember_us-gaap_OptionIndexedToIssuersEquityTypeAxis_us-gaap_CallOptionMember_A3D0uj5SckaMEFR7Ea74rQ" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:DebtInstrumentFaceAmount" scale="3" id="Narr_AE0ok0FNW0ydxO8zeYLBVg">1,000,000</ix:nonFraction> of Convertible Senior Notes to reduce the potential dilution to existing shareholders of the Company upon conversion of the Notes. The cap price of the capped call transactions is initially US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Divide_USD_shares_8k9rXZEOFkCLow36Uyv2xQ" contextRef="Duration_8_29_2022_To_8_29_2022_us-gaap_OptionIndexedToIssuersEquityTypeAxis_us-gaap_CallOptionMember_UI5GqkD2-0qDe8RYNl9O2A" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zto:OptionIndexedToIssuerSEquityStrikePriceCap" scale="0" id="Narr_0KbZLbMvuU6QvoOqArrvbQ">36.48</ix:nonFraction> per ADS, and is subject to adjustment under the terms of the capped call transactions. The total premium paid by the Company for the capped call options was RMB<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_CNY_xSGriXam1kKF-vMyssHgcw" contextRef="Duration_8_29_2022_To_8_29_2022_us-gaap_OptionIndexedToIssuersEquityTypeAxis_us-gaap_CallOptionMember_UI5GqkD2-0qDe8RYNl9O2A" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zto:OptionIndexedToIssuerSEquityPremium" scale="3" id="Narr_6nwdO8qXaEmxRIDpHm9qjg">373,139</ix:nonFraction> (equivalently US$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_USD_qF0kSPXROUmXco8Ic_aVpw" contextRef="Duration_8_29_2022_To_8_29_2022_us-gaap_OptionIndexedToIssuersEquityTypeAxis_us-gaap_CallOptionMember_UI5GqkD2-0qDe8RYNl9O2A" decimals="-3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zto:OptionIndexedToIssuerSEquityPremium" scale="3" id="Narr_sTxqOuF0o0iVo6xIPAxCrQ">54,000</ix:nonFraction>). The capped call options are classified as stockholders&#8217; equity and carried at the acquisition cost.</p></ix:continuation><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="font-size:1pt;margin-bottom:12pt;visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;margin:0pt;"><span style="visibility:hidden;">&#8203;</span></p><ix:nonNumeric contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_5thzZQv0lEmmjN0BhcOUQA" name="us-gaap:IncomeTaxDisclosureTextBlock" id="Tb_bdetA5L8Gk6a_FnLacrgiw" continuedAt="Tb_bdetA5L8Gk6a_FnLacrgiw_cont1" escape="true"><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;font-weight:bold;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">12. Income Tax </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">Under the current laws of the Cayman Islands, the Company is incorporated in the Cayman Islands and not subject to tax on income or capital gain. Additionally, the Cayman Islands does not impose a withholding tax on payments of dividends to shareholders. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">Under the current laws of the British Virgin Islands, the Company&#8217;s subsidiary incorporated in British Virgin Island is not subject to&#160;tax. </p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">Under the current Hong Kong Inland Revenue Ordinance, the Company&#8217;s subsidiaries domiciled in Hong Kong have applied a two-tiered profits tax rate regime. The profits tax rate for the first HK$<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_HKD_HWQQfcXEg0OEBhgBsWWHCA" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_HK_F19wUmYF20qNMntkTkou_w" decimals="-6" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:GrossProfit" scale="6" id="Narr_Mj3RuF4WVUGFx0t7wS45_Q">2</ix:nonFraction> million of profits of corporations is <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_XH5U-e4P3EyaYDdbgpgGqw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_RangeAxis_srt_MaximumMember_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_HK_LsSfMF4zf0uUZ-OpsYP6YA" decimals="4" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zto:IncomeTaxesForeignStatutoryCorporateTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_E_MTXoGQgUeqEwAnsudDGQ">8.25</ix:nonFraction>%, while profits above that amount is subject to the tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_XH5U-e4P3EyaYDdbgpgGqw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_HK_F19wUmYF20qNMntkTkou_w" decimals="3" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zto:IncomeTaxesForeignStatutoryCorporateTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_tBrQuPTS00yuDTZlnFyEYw">16.5</ix:nonFraction>%. Additionally, payments of dividends by the subsidiary incorporated in Hong Kong to the Company are not subject to any Hong Kong withholding tax.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">Under the Law of the People&#8217;s Republic of China on Enterprise Income Tax (&#8220;EIT&#160;Law&#8221;), the Company&#8217;s subsidiaries domiciled in the PRC are subject to statutory rate of&#160;<ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_XH5U-e4P3EyaYDdbgpgGqw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_srt_StatementGeographicalAxis_country_CN_xSM61PrExk2VhNql7rUh6Q" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="us-gaap:EffectiveIncomeTaxRateReconciliationAtFederalStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_-BAHlkXm5kaLNhjinOc7KQ">25</ix:nonFraction>%. Certain enterprises will benefit from a preferential tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_XH5U-e4P3EyaYDdbgpgGqw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_dei_EntitySectorIndustryClassificationsSectorAxis_zto_HighAndNewTechnologyEnterprisesMember_nZMy6aukyEWlVvsM1EBrcg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zto:PreferentialStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_bOsovqGDbUyn0nq46UGtoA">15</ix:nonFraction>% under the EIT Law if they qualify as &#8220;high and new technology enterprises,&#8221; or HNTEs, or if they are located in applicable PRC regions including Qianhai Shenzhen-Hong Kong Modern Service Industry Cooperation Zone, Hainan Free Trade Port, or regions as specified in the Catalogue of Encouraged Industries in Western Regions (effective till 2030), or the Western Regions Catalogue, subject to certain general restrictions described in the EIT Law and the related regulations.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;">WFOE is qualified for HNTE status and therefore eligible for a preferential income tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_XH5U-e4P3EyaYDdbgpgGqw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_dei_EntitySectorIndustryClassificationsSectorAxis_zto_WhollyOwnedForeignKeySoftwareEnterpriseMember_dei_LegalEntityAxis_zto_ShanghaiZhongtongjiExpressServiceCoLtdMember_Jbp4e-N6UkWnZg5Yes7l-w" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zto:PreferentialStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_yCu_HEq4HE-_7R0aoBBN0Q"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_XH5U-e4P3EyaYDdbgpgGqw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_dei_EntitySectorIndustryClassificationsSectorAxis_zto_WhollyOwnedForeignKeySoftwareEnterpriseMember_dei_LegalEntityAxis_zto_ShanghaiZhongtongjiExpressServiceCoLtdMember_Ij8uY1-uZUShpI32JMwfiQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zto:PreferentialStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_QzdB9jgs4EWeia9GmbG1NQ"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_XH5U-e4P3EyaYDdbgpgGqw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2025_To_12_31_2025_dei_EntitySectorIndustryClassificationsSectorAxis_zto_WhollyOwnedForeignKeySoftwareEnterpriseMember_dei_LegalEntityAxis_zto_ShanghaiZhongtongjiExpressServiceCoLtdMember_QRaVQ1TrxkKeY4w_q6UqQg" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zto:PreferentialStatutoryIncomeTaxRate" scale="-2" id="Narr_61xtVVLZDUKdIR9yhlK_lw">15</ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction></ix:nonFraction>% for the years ended December 31, 2023, 2024 and 2025. In addition, WFOE applied for the Key Software Enterprise status in early 2023 and 2025. After the approval by the relevant tax authority in 2023 and 2025, WFOE was entitled to a preferential tax rate of <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_pure_XH5U-e4P3EyaYDdbgpgGqw" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024_dei_EntitySectorIndustryClassificationsSectorAxis_zto_WhollyOwnedForeignKeySoftwareEnterpriseMember_dei_LegalEntityAxis_zto_ShanghaiZhongtongjiExpressServiceCoLtdMember_Ij8uY1-uZUShpI32JMwfiQ" decimals="2" format="ixt:num-dot-decimal" name="zto:DecreasedPreferentialStatutoryIncomeTaxRates" scale="-2" id="Narr_qTktqQ2JkUuoQazw21hSsA">10</ix:nonFraction>% retroactively for the years ended December 31, 2022 and 2024.</p><p style="font-family:'Times New Roman','Times','serif';font-size:10pt;text-align:justify;text-indent:36pt;margin:0pt 0pt 10pt 0pt;"><ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_company_d69GWRvcakq9bgT1NlUGMQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2023_To_12_31_2023_43j8GFpS4EOQU4KWXlrdtQ" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="zto:NumberOfSubsidiariesWhichAreLocatedInMunicipalitiesObtainedApprovalFromLocalTaxAuthorities" scale="0" id="Narr_vYGuXpHQ0k6YYE3yXLOUNA">Six</ix:nonFraction>, <ix:nonFraction unitRef="Unit_Standard_company_d69GWRvcakq9bgT1NlUGMQ" contextRef="Duration_1_1_2024_To_12_31_2024__-ZOoP7FxUq9HeZ38HqV6Q" decimals="INF" format="ixt-sec:numwordsen" name="zto:NumberOfSubsidiariesWhichAreLocatedInMunicipalitiesObtainedApprovalFromLocalTaxAuthorities" scale="0" id="Narr_h